   "note": "The rule says `right now`, and a certificate that expires in three days is not broken yet, so the second reader labelled it `no`; the stored label reads a fixed deadline inside the queue's turnaround as urgent. The rule does not say how an imminent failure counts."
  },
  {
   "id": "urgency/043",
   "family": "urgency",
   "partition": "development",
   "stored": "no",
   "second": "yes",
   "agree": false,
   "note": "The rule says `broken, blocked, or unsafe right now`, and a down test environment blocks the team that uses it, so the second reader labelled it `yes`; the stored label weighs the absence of production impact. The rule does not say whose breakage counts."
  }
